---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Find Local's privacy policy: no accounts, no third-party analytics, no advertising cookies. What little data exists stays in your browser." canonicalPath="/privacy">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="faint"><em>Last updated: September 4, 2026</em></p>
    <p>
      Welcome to Find Local ("Find Local," "we," "us," or "our"). This Privacy Policy explains what information is (and isn't)
      collected when you use the website findlocal.community (the "Service"). The short version: there are no user accounts,
      we run no third-party analytics or advertising trackers, and the only data about your preferences lives in your own browser.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Nothing you have to give us.</strong> The Service has no registration, login, profiles or social features. You can use every part of it without telling us who you are.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Preferences stored in your browser.</strong> Your chosen city (a cookie named <code>fl_city</code>) and any events you save are stored on your device using cookies and browser storage. They are used to render the pages you request and are not sent to us for any other purpose or linked to an identity.</li>
      <li><strong>Log and usage data.</strong> Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) automatically records standard technical information for security and reliability when you access the Service, such as IP address, browser type and pages requested. This data is processed in aggregate and is not linked to an identified person.</li>
      <li><strong>Communications.</strong> If you email us, we receive whatever you choose to send.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, operate and maintain the Service (for example, showing events for your chosen city).</li>
      <li>To keep the Service secure and reliable.</li>
      <li>To understand aggregate usage (for example, page views by country) and improve the Service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Affiliate links and third-party commissions</h2>
    <p>
      The Service may contain affiliate links to third-party websites, venues or ticketing services. Find Local may receive a
      commission if you make a purchase through these links, regardless of whether the purchase is made immediately after
      clicking or later. This does not affect your privacy or the price you pay.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Automated access and data scraping</h2>
    <p>
      Using automated means to collect data from the Service beyond what our <code>robots.txt</code> allows is prohibited
      without our written permission. Developers who want structured access should use the <a href="/platform">Find Local platform</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Analytics and tracking technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Find Local does not use third-party analytics or session-recording tools such as Google Analytics or Microsoft Clarity,
      and does not set advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. Our hosting provider may collect privacy-preserving,
      aggregate traffic metrics that do not use cookies or identify individual visitors. If we introduce analytics tooling in
      the future, we will update this policy first.
    </p>
    <p>
      Embedded maps load tiles from OpenStreetMap only when a map is on screen; OpenStreetMap's own <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> applies to those requests.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How we share information</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal data. We share information only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>With service providers</strong> that run the Service on our behalf (web hosting and database infrastructure from Cloudflare), who may access it only to perform those tasks.</li>
      <li><strong>As aggregated, anonymized data</strong> that does not identify anyone.</li>
      <li><strong>For legal reasons</strong>, if required by law or a valid request from a public authority.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Your rights and data control</h2>
    <p>
      Because preferences are stored on your device, you control them directly: clear your browser's cookies and site data
      for findlocal.community to remove them. If you have contacted us by email and want that correspondence deleted, ask us.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is not directed to children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.
      Users must meet the legal age required in their jurisdiction to attend events involving alcohol or other
      age-restricted activities.
    </p>

    <h2>9. California and European users</h2>
    <p>
      Residents of California (CCPA) and data subjects in the European Economic Area (GDPR) have rights to access, correct,
      delete and port personal data, and to object to or restrict certain processing. Given that we hold no account data,
      requests will normally concern email correspondence; contact us at the address below and we will comply with all
      applicable laws and verifiable requests. Find Local does not sell personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the new policy on this page and update the "Last updated" date.</p>

    <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:findlocalinternal@gmail.com">findlocalinternal@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
